          <div class="item_d">
            <h4 class="sub_title_name">Aparna Kakrania</h4>
            <h5>Brand Builder. Designer. Storyteller.</h5>
            <div class="desc">
               For over 28 years, Aparna Kakrania has been at the intersection of design, business, and narrative. As the founder of Design Dimensions- her design studio, she has carved a niche for herself in the world of visual communication- building strategies, crafting identities, shaping brand worlds, and telling stories that linger.<br>
              At Design Dimensions, Aparna leads with intention. She works closely with homegrown Indian brands-some steeped in legacy, some just beginning their journeys-to help them discover and express who they really are. Her approach is immersive, intuitive, and always grounded in story.<br>
              Over the years, Aparna has worked with a long list of clients, each one bringing with them a story waiting to be told. Her work on Suryagarh Jaisalmer, stands as a hallmark - where she reimagined the brand story, communication design, and interior styling of this luxurious desert retreat, while weaving in local crafts through thoughtfully designed merchandise. For White Rhino, India's pioneering craft beer, Aparna created a 360 degree brand world - from identity to tone of voice - helping define the category itself. With Papadmalji, she brought design-driven thinking to a traditional Bikaneri food brand, balancing legacy with a modern visual language. With The Kachori Story, a playful QSR concept, she shaped every touchpoint - from branding and storytelling to the spatial design experience. Most recently, she worked with Diageo on Godawan, the company's first Indian single malt whisky, where she led craft storytelling and merchandise design inspired by Rajasthan's landscape, heritage, and artisan culture.<br>
              At the heart of all her work is craft. For Aparna, craft is not a trend - it is tradition, provenance, and presence. It is tactile, emotional, and layered with meaning. Her designs are deeply considered, yet quietly expressive - always reflective of time, place, and people. "Craft isn't massy,"" she says. "It's intimate."<br>
              As a designer and storyteller, Aparna brings empathy and instinct into every brief. As an entrepreneur, she has built a studio that values originality over scale, and depth over noise. In a world of fast design, she stands for what endures-stories told with soul, and brands built to last.
            </div>
